    },
    {
      "commit": "684f7407de676afc8cf3054a3f45557296db4592",
      "title": "fix: wireless ADB page names the child-process switch the way Android shows it",
      "summary": "The wireless ADB page now names the Developer options switch the way Android shows it: \"Turn on \u201cDisable child process restrictions\u201d\" to lift the limit, and \"Turn off ...\" to put it back. It used to tell users to set \"Restrict child processes\" on or off, which is not a switch Android shows.",
